flowchart LR

REQ["`POST — create a subject
Traefik receives, routes by hostname,
attaches the real client IP,
forwards to FastAPI`"]

M1["`security headers`"]
M2["`request logs
records even the
requests that were blocked`"]
M3["`rate limiter`"]
M4["`CSRF`"]

MWNOTE["`Starlette runs the LAST registered
middleware FIRST — so security headers
decorate every response, including
the 429 returned by the rate limiter`"]

VAL["`ROUTER + VALIDATION
body checked against the declared shape
malformed body → 422, before any
application code runs`"]

DI["`DEPENDENCY INJECTION
builds the service and hands it a
request-scoped database session,
the repository and the audit writer`"]

REPO["`REPOSITORY — commands data access
filters by owner and by non-deleted
rows (soft delete)
database access uses the ORM
with parameters`"]

TX["`ONE TRANSACTION
service creates the row tied to the
authenticated user AND writes the audit
line · PostgreSQL commits both together —
no 'log says success, operation failed'
every business action writes a line`"]

OUT["`RESPONSE
model serialized to the response shape
middleware adds the headers
one structured log line: acting user
+ trace identifier`"]

AUTH["`LOGIN — three cookies
access token 15 min · refresh token 30 days
both HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite
CSRF is the only non-HttpOnly one
tokens hashed SHA-256 in the database
refresh ROTATED · reuse of a revoked token
ends ALL sessions (reuse detection)
Argon2id for passwords · login-attempt
lockout · account export and deletion`"]

OAUTH["`OAUTH + OIDC — many doors, one house
Google · Microsoft · Apple on one account
callback routes registered ONLY when the
provider is configured · scopes: openid,
email, profile — OIDC hands IDENTITY,
not just authorization · one-time state
both paths end in the SAME authorization`"]

REQ --> M1 --> M2 --> M3 --> M4
M4 -.- MWNOTE
M4 --> VAL --> DI --> REPO --> TX --> OUT
AUTH -.-|"guards every request"| REQ
AUTH -.- OAUTH

